  {
   "symbol": "d",
   "kind": "note",
   "props": {
    "flag": "c11_duarte",
    "text": "STATEMENT OF CPL. INES DUARTE, POST ONE\nSEALED BY ORDER OF THE DIRECTORATE — 18 OCT 1998\n\nAt approximately 02:46 Technician M. Solace came up in the service lift carrying the Director's son. She was crying. She put him in my arms and pinned a card to his blanket. The card said: HIS NAME IS DANIEL. DON'T LET THEM BRING HIM BACK HERE.\n\nShe said: 'Drive. Don't stop. Don't turn the radio on.'\n\nShe went back down. I watched the lights in the shaft go out floor by floor, like something was eating them.\n\nI drove. I did not turn the radio on. At the bottom of the mountain it turned itself on, and it was her voice, saying thank you.\n\nI did not stop.\n\nThe boy was placed with the county. I asked that his name be changed. I asked that nobody ever tell him where he came from.\n\nI am told the family is called Arlen.",
    "title": "Sealed statement — Cpl. I. Duarte"
   },
   "sequence": -1,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "e",
   "kind": "note",
   "props": {
    "text": "VAULT D — DIRECTOR\n\nCombination per Dr. Voss: 'It opens at the moment it all ends.'\n\n(Below, in Hale's hand:)\nThat's not a combination, Evelyn. That's a threat.\n\n(Below that, in hers:)\nIt's both, Marcus. Most things are.",
    "title": "Taped to the Director's vault"
   },
   "sequence": -1,
   "lines": -1
  },
