 "sequences": [
  {
   "steps": [
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "PA",
      "Current time: zero two — forty-three."
     ],
     "vo": "pa_f40e4bfbe4"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "The Archive. Every page this place ever printed, every tape it ever cut."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_ba0c6f5b4a"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "Hale kept a vault down here. So did she. If there's a truth in this mountain, it's on a shelf."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_2bfabb2ecb"
    },
    {
     "command": "toast",
     "args": [
      "It has learned how you hide and where you go. Now it waits for you."
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "obj",
     "args": [
      "The deep lift needs the archive keycard and the Director's voiceprint. Read the index card. Look for the vaults."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "steps": [
    {
     "command": "journal",
     "args": [
      "Run 19 — operational order",
      "RUN 19 — OPERATIONAL ORDER\nAuthorised: E. Voss, Director\nSecurity sign-off: REFUSED — M. Hale\n\nHale: 'I will not sign. There is a child on this level, and a thing on this channel that asks for him by a name he doesn't have yet. If you run it, Evelyn, run it without him.'\n\nVoss (pencil): 'Mira takes him up at 02:40. You have my word.'\n\nRun commenced: 02:40.\nNo record of the child leaving the level before 02:43."
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "give",
     "args": [
      "battery"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "give",
     "args": [
      "medkit"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "sfx",
     "args": [
      "pickup",
      "-6"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "toast",
     "args": [
      "Taken: Power cell, Medkit"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "'Run it without him.' Hale tried. Hale was the only one who tried."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_8ebd326e9c"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "steps": [
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "PELL (1998)",
      "Tunde. I asked him his name."
     ],
     "vo": "pell_f58e96354a"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "OKAFOR (1998)",
      "And?"
     ],
     "vo": "okafor_8ff36896f8"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "PELL (1998)",
      "He said Arlen. Then he said, 'Is anyone still there?' — and he wasn't. He just wasn't, Tunde. Like a station going off the air."
     ],
     "vo": "pell_5ab436dd3b"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "OKAFOR (1998)",
      "...Forty-two."
     ],
     "vo": "okafor_01c02d3f49"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "PELL (1998)",
      "What?"
     ],
     "vo": "pell_2342ed5242"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "OKAFOR (1998)",
      "I've counted forty-two all night. Now I know who the extra one was."
     ],
     "vo": "okafor_570f864f28"
    },
    {
     "command": "ach",
     "args": [
      "pell"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "journal",
     "args": [
      "The forty-second",
      "In 1998, Jonah Pell followed a man in an orange jacket through HELIX-9 — the open-plan office, Lind's records, the Signal Room, the Archive. He asked the man his name. The man said Arlen.\n\nOkafor had counted forty-two people all night. The forty-second was me."
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
